GtkACE 0.3.0 (2026-11-07)

  Intelligence on other countries:
  - Output of your commands is read for sightings, as WinACE does:
    lookout, llook, coastwatch, skywatch, sonar and spy reports (and
    anything else printing the same lines).  Sectors and units seen are
    kept in the game database with the time and the command that saw
    them.
  - Other countries' sectors are drawn in their player colours.  Their
    ships, land units and planes use WinACE's icons: red for countries
    you are at war with or hostile to, green for friendly or allied,
    blue for neutral, and grey for sightings more than a day old.
  - The sector panel shows what was seen of a foreign sector (owner,
    efficiency, people, stocks, roads, defence) and when, and lists
    foreign units seen there.
  - Units window has a Foreign tab (Ctrl+5) listing every sighting.
  - Reports -> Intelligence menu: lookout, land lookout, radar, land
    radar, sonar, coastwatch, skywatch, spy.
  - File -> Clear Intelligence forgets all sightings.
  - Relations are read from the server, and re-read after declare.
  Fixes:
  - Server tables with array fields (such as relations) are now stored
    correctly: one column per element.

GtkACE 0.2.0 (2026-11-07)

  Units:
  - Ships, land units, planes and nukes are read from the server (xdump)
    and drawn on the map with WinACE's unit icons; View menu switches
    each kind on or off.
  - New Units window (Units menu, Ctrl+1 to Ctrl+4): sortable lists of
    ships, land units, planes and nukes with location, efficiency,
    mobility, tech, cargo, fleet/army/wing and what each is loaded on.
    Double-click a unit to find it on the map.
  - The sector panel lists the units in the selected sector.
  - Right-click menu lists the ships, land units or planes in a sector.
  - Units menu also runs cargo, lcargo, sstat, lstat, pstat and show build.
  - Refresh -> Update Units.
  Other:
  - After commands that change sectors or units (move, navigate, build,
    designate, load, fly ...), GtkACE quietly re-reads sectors, units and
    the bmap so the map stays current.
  - Table descriptions are fetched once per login, so refreshes send
    less traffic.

GtkACE 0.1.0 (2026-11-07)

  First release: a port of WinACE 2.5.72 to C and GTK 3.
  - Game list and login dialog; async connect and Empire login.
  - Command line with history, server questions, Escape to abort.
  - Telegram/announcement notices and AutoRead.
  - SQLite database built from xdump; bmap parsing.
  - Hex map with sector details panel and right-click commands.
  - Offline mode; report menus and toolbar.
  Tested against Wolfpack Empire 4.4.0.
